# Intentionally empty.
#
# Fingerprints here are keyed by `<sha>:<file>:<rule>:<line>`, so the #111
# history rewrite invalidated every one of them at once and left the scheduled
# Security workflow red (#145) -- and the action scans `--all`, which reaches
# tags and abandoned branches whose SHAs no rewrite of master can ever restate.
# The commit-less form gitleaks also accepts, `<file>:<rule>:<line>`, survives a
# rewrite but is still positional: it would suppress a real credential that
# later lands on that line, in that file, under that rule. Neither belongs here.
#
# There is nothing left for it to hold anyway. No tracked file spells out an
# armor header -- every marker is assembled at run time (`src/utils/armor.ts`,
# `client/**/armor_test.go`, `armor()` in `scripts/key-size.py`) or described
# rather than printed (`API.md`, `DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md`, `docs/github-app.md`) --
# so the detector does not fire on a fixture and there is nothing to excuse.
# `scripts/test-gitleaks-contract.sh` proves it, by scanning the tree with
# `.gitleaks.toml` and with a bare `useDefault` config and requiring the two to
# agree.
#
# If a scan reports something new, classify it, and change the fixture's
# representation rather than suppressing it. Do not add a fingerprint here.
